- `Shape` inherits from `ABC` (Abstract Base Class) and declares an abstract method `area`. Any subclass must implement `area`, otherwise instantiation will raise a `TypeError`.
- `Circle` stores a radius, validates it, and computes the area with \(πr^2\).  
- `Rectangle` stores width and height, validates them, and computes the area with \(width × height\).  
- Both concrete classes provide a `__repr__` for readable debugging.

